WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.933
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 3, Network operations, which is 19 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:10.687
This lesson covers objective 3 point 5.

00:00:10.687 --> 00:00:14.854
Compare and contrast network access and management methods.

00:00:14.854 --> 00:00:17.820
Today's concept is out-of-band management.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:25.857
Normally an admin manages a switch over the same production network that carries everyone's traffic.

00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:26.710
That's in-band.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:33.326
Out-of-band adds a second, dedicated path, like a console server, that does not depend on production.

00:00:33.326 --> 00:00:34.885
Independence is the test.

00:00:34.885 --> 00:00:38.750
A management VLAN on the production switches is still in-band.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.164
Now the production network fails.

00:00:41.164 --> 00:00:42.750
The in-band path is gone.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:48.310
But the admin can still reach the switch, because the dedicated path never touched production.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:55.540
For the exam, out-of-band means a dedicated path that is independent of production.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.175
If the network is down and you can still manage the device, that's out-of-band.

00:01:00.175 --> 00:01:02.170
That's objective three point five.
